LANDING PR for story #362, fourth landing (the CLI reference, generated from clap, and every documented brokkr command parsed).

The branch story-362-cli-reference ends at e9286a77 on main 577176bb. The third landing (landing-pr-for-story-362-third-l-3800bf68) shipped clean at e140e577: its fix makes the fence gate refuse a cargo run that gives its package or a run option twice (with -q and --quiet as one), which cargo itself refuses before any brokkr runs. The controller's exact-coverage gate then found one function of 3,378 not run, with lines and branches whole. It was rerun's "loading source run" context, left unreached once --run is resolved through the selector before the load. The controller's commit e9286a77 adds verbs::tests::rerun_names_a_resolved_run_it_cannot_load (a selector-resolved run with a broken chain), with its removal control recorded. It changes no production code.

OPERATOR RULING (2026-09-29), binding: the exact whole-line allowlist NAMED_NOT_RUN is ACCEPTED for the four documented non-run cargo lines (cargo binstall brokkr-cli; cargo install --path crates/brokkr-cli; cargo test --locked -p brokkr-cli --test suppressions; cargo build --release --locked -p brokkr-cli). It is not a finding.

Everything the earlier landings confirmed stands:
- the reference is byte-compared to clap;
- empty descriptions are refused;
- the structural rule refuses any unparsed mention of brokkr in a living-doc fence;
- cargo() is closed-world, and a repeated package or run option is refused;
- the selector table binds both ways;
- every --run resolves through the selector;
- the exit codes are one enum.

Judge:
1. That e9286a77 is a test only, binds what it claims (the rerun's context text and the store's cause), and leaves no production path unreached.
2. That no cargo line in a living doc can run brokkr without its arguments reaching Cli::try_parse_from, or pass while running no brokkr at all, outside the four ruled exact lines.

This run lands one pull request under decision 0051 so the contribution gate can vouch for it. If a finding returns the branch, fix exactly that finding and prove it with a test bound by a compiling mutation. Then run cargo fmt --all -- --check, cargo clippy on the crates you touched with -D warnings, typos --hidden, and quality/ratchet.sh files and clones (all clean). Commit one signed-off commit ending "Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>", and never push. Do not run scripts/coverage-exact.sh; the controller runs it.

Threat model (operator ruling, 2026-09-26): catch realistic accidental misuse, and fail closed on what cannot be read.
